# Discord Activity credentials. Copy to `.env` and fill in from
# https://discord.com/developers/applications → your app → OAuth2.
#
# Neither is needed to play Deep Field on a plain URL over Tailscale — the game
# runs without this file at all. They are only read when the page is opened
# inside Discord, which is detected by the `frame_id` parameter Discord adds.
#
# `.env` is gitignored explicitly (see .gitignore — the `*.local` rule does NOT
# cover it, which is worth knowing before you trust it). Never put a real secret
# in this file: it is the one that is committed.

# Public. Vite inlines this into the client bundle, where anyone can read it.
# That is how OAuth2 client ids work and is not a leak.
VITE_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# Server-side only, and genuinely secret. Read by server/index.ts to trade the
# Activity's one-time code for an access token. If this ever appears in a client
# bundle, rotate it immediately: anything holding it can act as your app.
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
